 "question": "How does OpenHands isolate execution (container runtime, action/observation loop) and how do its microagents get triggered — and is the trigger mechanism a better router than keyword matching?",
 "title": "Teardown of OpenHands runtime isolation and its microagent trigger model",
 "canonical_mechanism": "DockerWorkspace container + Agent.step action/observation; auto-trigger is Skill.match_trigger at openhands-sdk/openhands/sdk/skills/skill.py:732 (keyword/path match, not an LLM router).",
 "answer": "Execution isolation: optional DockerWorkspace starts `docker run -d --rm` of an OpenHands agent-server image and proxies tools through that container HTTP API. The loop is Agent.step -> tool action -> ObservationEvent. Microagent/skill auto-trigger is Skill.match_trigger (openhands-sdk/openhands/sdk/skills/skill.py:732) plus PathTrigger globs — identical string matching for KeywordTrigger and TaskTrigger. It is not a better router than keyword matching; it is keyword matching. Failure mode: GitHub issue #10073 (slash-prefixed triggers such as /design not firing, including after type: knowledge).",
 "completion_sentinel": "SUCCESS:RES-0029 in the receipt AND the trigger implementation cited at file:line plus one issue-tracker-sourced failure mode",
